      "latex": "\\clearpage\n\\centerline{\\bfseries\\Large Notation}\n\\begin{itemize}\n  \\item For a set $A$, $x\\in A$ means ``$x$ is an element of $A$''; $|A|$ is the number of elements of $A$.\n  \\item $A \\setminus B$ is the set of elements of $A$ that are not in $B$.\n  \\item $\\mathbb{N}=\\{1,2,3,\\ldots\\}$ is the set of natural numbers, $\\mathbb{Z}$ the set of integers and $\\mathbb{R}$ the set of real numbers.\n  \\item For $a,b\\in\\mathbb{R}$: $[a,b]=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\mid a\\le x\\le b\\}$ and $(a,b)=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\mid a<x<b\\}$; $a\\mid b$ means ``$a$ divides $b$''.\n  \\item $n!=n\\cdot(n-1)\\cdots 2\\cdot 1$, and $\\lfloor x\\rfloor$ is the largest integer not greater than $x$.\n  \\item $[ABC]$ is the area of triangle $ABC$.\n\\end{itemize}\n\\vspace{2ex}\\hrule\\vspace{2ex}"
